==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-root|م|س|ك}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|form=I|head=مَسَكَ|tr=másaka}}

# to [[grab]], [[grasp]], [[clutch]], [[clasp]], [[seize]], [[take hold]]
# to [[hold]]
# to [[stick]], [[cling]], [[adhere]], [[hang on]]
# to [[keep]] ''(the books, accounts, etc.)''
# to [[take]] ''(charge, control, etc.)''

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|form=II|head=مَسَّكَ|tr=mássaka}}

# to have someone [[seize]] or [[hold]] something

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|head=مَسْك|tr=mask|g=m}}

# [[seizure]], [[grip]], [[hold]]
# [[keeping]] ''(bookkeeping, etc.)''

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|head=مُسُك|tr=músuk|g=m|pl=مسكة|plhead=مُسَكَة|pltr=músaka}}

# [[grasping]], [[greedy]], [[avaricious]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|fa|ar}} {{term|مشک|tr=mošk|lang=fa||musk}}, from {{etyl|pal|ar}} {{term|𐭬𐭥𐭱𐭪𐭩|tr=mušk|lang=pal||musk}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|form=II|head=مَسَّكَ|tr=mássaka}}

# to [[scent]] with [[musk]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|head=مِسْك|tr=misk|g=m|g2=f}}

# [[musk]]

